data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","item_id":"rs_02f658e8d3cdfa94016acaa730bb20819381d67767fa78e551","output_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Implementing server-rendered forms**\n\nI’m thinking about how to create server-rendered HTML forms without needing JavaScript, so it should work fine with a browser stack that supports HTML, CSS, and absent JavaScript. APIs aren’t required, but I need to test it using node spawn for persistence. There will be routes for POST and GET requests for projects, ensuring proper validation, visible alerts, and styling. I should also consider DB path directories and a generic body size handler along with proper timing."},"sequence_number":99,"summary_index":0}

